{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1415417-divine-powers","id":1415417,"title":"Divine powers?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-09-25T08:08:43-07:00","id":1415417,"title":"Divine powers?","content":"Do you know vampric divine powers? I mean those can manifest or even bring divine essence (Sun, Sunlight, True Faith, etc.)<br /> <br /> For example, Eye of Unforgiving Heaven (Auspex 4, Warrior Valeren 4) in DAV20, which can manifest user\u2019s virtue as sunlight I think Salubri (or Baali?!) may have some tricks, but I don\u2019t have books at my hand<br /> <br /> Tip: Maybe some messiah or satanic methseulahs know ritual can make Sun raise at midnight\u2026","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24560,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24560-rock113","user":"Rock113","date":". 09-25-2020, 11:24 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24560-rock113","name":"Rock113","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24560_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-29T14:56:54-07:00","id":1416032,"title":"","content":"Chimerstry can emulate such powers. But this will be illusion or distortion of reality.<br /> Sadhana: path of karma.<br /> I remember there is one combo discipline obtenebration and valeren (or fortitude?), It allows you to resist the dark forces.<br /> Certain Sabbat rituals, though more related to worship of Cain.<br /> <br /> Also. There is some true-faith powers. It can give you second immortality.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25408,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25408-alphari","user":"Alphari","date":". 09-30-2020, 07:46 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25408-alphari","name":"Alphari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25408_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"153"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-30T05:55:50-07:00","id":1416093,"title":"","content":"I'm curious what divine powers do they have. I mean: summon celestial beings (Elohim?), bring sunlight or even Sun itself, etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24560-rock113","name":"Rock113","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24560_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-30T06:48:22-07:00","id":1416097,"title":"","content":"Elohim? Kraina of the Well. Maybe some form of Dark-Thaumaturgy and (potentially) high level of Daimonion in Devils Due<span style=\"font-family:arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-size:28px\">.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> If you are asking about the powers I have listed:\u200b<br /> <br /> 1) Sadhana - Karma allows you to remember your past life, one of your past incarnations. It also allows you to change your character (temporarily) and remember some skills &amp; knowledge. Cainites can remember their mortal lifes. Feel alive and even bring this life back for one night.<br /> <br /> You can also see your own or someone else's karma. It also lets you know if the mortal will become a Katayan, a ghost or transcend. This allows you to see your future incarnation, to know your destiny (the possible death to which you or another is going ... unless you change your fate). This allows Cainites to correct karma for their ghouls so that they can live good next-life later.<br /> <br /> But this is a very difficult magic. If I am not mistaken, some phenomena are very difficult to invoke.<br /> <br /> 2) Chimerstry - Summon an illusory angel and let him judge enemies. Or call on an illusory demon to pursue sinners. Or create this illusion and make it real if you are ancient vamp.<br /> <br /> 3) Combo-dis: Vicente de las Navas de Tolosa's Holy Shield - Obten 2 + Fortitude 1 =&gt; There are suspicions that this was cut from DAV20. But somewhere on this form you can still find full description. I find this discipline strange and too OP.<br /> <br /> 4) I don't know much about Sabbath rituals. But, I remember that there were rituals that allowed you to get twice as much blood during a certain holiday. Also there was a ritual that gives you the mark of Cain. This gives you an analogue of True Faith, but you must believe in Cain. Also, it is connected with some paths of enlightenment.<br /> <br /> I also remember that these rituals are associated with the faith and power in Cain's blood.<br /> <br /> 5-1) True Faith:<br /> <br /> There are some artifacts - items, water, shrine. Sometimes they require some action. Sometimes they require certain paths of enlightenment, rolls of courage &amp; etc. They don't require True Faith. These artifacts have their own True Faith rating. And some may even endow you with the True Faith - the Altar of Ra (I understand that it gives first dot &amp; some sun-resistence).<br /> <br /> 5-2) Biblical Necromancy:<br /> <br /> This is a group of rituals. These rituals only work if the Cainite holds the appropriate faith, there is a chance that some of these rituals could be adapted to other faiths. But this requires the approval of ST. (Because this is not a copying of rituals or mixing of beliefs ... this is important.)<br /> <br /> Exampls:<br /> <br /> <b>Lazarus Rises <span style=\"font-size:18px\">\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 \u2022</span></b>: &quot;<i>Variations of this ritual are known under many names: Lazarus Rises, Hades Rejects, and Ma\u2019at Is Blinded are the most common ones. The <b>necromancer </b>tattoos a <b>Cainite target</b> with tiny <b>symbols denoting her faith</b>, while <b>lining a room with the same script</b>. When the target would suffer Final Death, he instead disappears in a cloud of ashes and reappears \u2014 albeit in torpor \u2014 in the prepared room. The rules of torpor then apply to him normally, and clever vampires make sure to have a devoted servant guard the room in case it\u2019s ever needed. This ritual has a duration of a year and a day, regardless of whether it\u2019s invoked or not, and may only be cast on the target once during that time. For example, the necromancer can re-cast if her target goes without incident for a year and two days. If the ritual is invoked a week in, though, he must wait the full remaining year and a day before the necromancer may extend her protection to him again.&quot;</i><br /> <br /> Restoration of Styx <span style=\"font-size:18px\"><b>\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022</b></span>: <i>&quot;Necromancy is a foul tool that corrupts everything it touches with darkness from beyond the grave. In the hands of the righteous though, it can soothe those who have one foot across the river of death: vampires, ghosts, and mummies. The necromancer uses one blood point\u2019s worth of her own blood to anoint her target with symbols of healing. She then<b> rolls her Necromancy</b> as usual, and heals her target\u2019s wounds, up to a number of bashing and lethal health levels equal to her successes. Alternatively, she may spend an extra Willpower to heal him of half her successes (rounded up) in aggravated health levels instead. The Necromancer cannot use this ritual on herself.&quot;</i><br /> <br /> I have a suspicion that we should use standard rules for necromancy rituals =&gt; Religion/Occult + Intelligence Diff: 8 (3 + 5 Faith-level)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25408,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25408-alphari","user":"Alphari","date":". 09-30-2020, 11:03 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25408-alphari","name":"Alphari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25408_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"153"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-30T07:04:44-07:00","id":1416099,"title":"","content":"I always think that should be level 10 (or at least level 9) effect, for only Caine himself met true Elohim","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24560-rock113","name":"Rock113","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24560_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-30T08:14:43-07:00","id":1416103,"title":"","content":"Technically and potentially... Cainite can also get an Avatar shard or borrow Avatar of another magician.<br /> If vamp is lucky, mage might be a priest or belong to some religious group. In old editions it was written that Celestial Chorus magic is capable of inflicting aggravate damage <i>(Or is it more difficult for &quot;evil&quot; factions to defend against such magic? I don't remember well, I'm not a mage-fan)</i> to Nefandi or evil spirits (demons). But it was in some old book of the Dark Ages, maybe Sorcerers Crusade (but I don't remember).<br /> <br /> Daimonion also have some fire-sun damage power (or powers).<br /> <b>Unleash Hell's Fury</b>: Cause a Cainite to feel the sun's light no matter what shelter they have.<br /> <b>Adramelech's Warth</b>: Vampire calls down power of Adramelech, demon associeted with sun. Vampire (target) will suffer sun-damage as if vampire stand outside at high-noon. Couse R\u00f6tschreck. Victim glows white hot &amp; provokes R\u00f6tschreck for Baali every turn while maintaining this power.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25408,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25408-alphari","user":"Alphari","date":". 09-30-2020, 12:31 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25408-alphari","name":"Alphari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25408_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"153"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}